trait-centaur-rule-basics = STR +3, INT −2, WIS +1, DEX +2, CON +1; life 103%, base HP 22, experience requirement 190%.
trait-centaur-rule-speed = Gain 1 speed every 10 levels and cross forest vegetation without the usual extra walking time.
trait-centaur-rule-armor = Cannot wear boots. Body armor loses one third of its base armor and one third of positive armor enchantment, each rounded toward zero. Negative enchantments remain in full.
trait-centaur-rule-hooves = Hooves add attacks after ordinary melee, including when unarmed. Dice, accuracy, damage and attack rate grow with level and attributes, up to two attacks per round. Proficiency starts at 4000 and caps at 8000; using hooves against sufficiently strong foes can train it even on a miss.
trait-centaur-rule-power = At level 15, gain Jump: DEX, cost 10, base failure 50%. Range is 2 + level / 35, rounded down. Jump over intervening monsters to a destination in line of sight that permits teleportation. Anti-teleport blocks movement but still spends resources.
trait-centaur-rule-birth = Keep class equipment, ordinary food and light. The racial virtue is Nature. Cavalry is unavailable.
trait-balrog-rule-basics = STR +4, INT +2, WIS −10, DEX +2, CON +3, CHR +2; life 106%, base HP 24, experience requirement 180%.
trait-balrog-rule-defenses = A nonliving demon with fire and nether resistance, hold life and infravision 5. See invisible from level 10; gain stronger fire resistance at level 45, without immunity. Cannot bleed or become unwell.
trait-balrog-rule-alignment = Alignment −200 affects realm spell failure and holy or hellfire damage. The racial virtue is Justice.
trait-balrog-rule-diet = Sacrifice a human corpse in your pack or at your feet to become fully fed, consuming one corpse. Ordinary food and native potion nutrition provide only one twentieth. Inns provide fresh meat.
trait-balrog-rule-power = At level 15, gain Breathe Fire/Nether: CON, base failure 70%, cost 10 + level / 3. Each successful cast chooses fire or nether equally, dealing level × 3 damage in a cone with radius 1 + level / 15. Divisions round down; spell power and target resistance apply.
trait-balrog-rule-birth = Begin with 3–4 human corpses and light, alongside class equipment. Human corpses come from creatures displayed as p, h or t; skeletons cannot be sacrificed.
trait-android-rule-basics = STR +3, INT −1, WIS −5, DEX +1, CON +3; 108% life and +26 base HP.
trait-android-rule-experience = Your current equipment determines experience and level. Equipping, enchanting and equipment damage can raise or lower your level. Rings, amulets and lights contribute nothing. Kills and potions give no experience; regaining a level does not repeat attribute rewards.
trait-android-rule-defenses = Nonliving, poison resistance, free action, hold life and slow digestion. Gain 10 + level × 2 / 5 AC. Electrical resistance provides 70% of its usual damage reduction; immunity is unchanged.
trait-android-rule-diet = Drink oil from your pack or the ground for 5000 nutrition. Ordinary food gives none; potions provide 1/20 nutrition in your native form.
trait-android-rule-power = Levels 1 / 10 / 25 / 35 / 45 select Ray Gun, Blaster, Bazooka, Beam Cannon or Rocket Launcher. Only the current stage is available, including after losing levels. Powers use STR and cost 7 / 13 / 26 / 40 / 60.
trait-android-rule-birth = Start with 7–12 oil flasks, light and one fifth of normal gold. Body armor is omitted from starting equipment.
