guide-help = Help (?)
guide-knowledge = Knowledge (~)
guide-help-intro = Controls for the current version. Your active preset is shown above; Original/Roguelike instructions apply only to those presets. / focuses search, Tab moves focus, Enter opens a chapter, and Esc closes this manual. Reading help or knowledge costs no turn.
guide-search = Search titles and text
guide-contents = Help contents
guide-no-results = No matching chapters. Try another term or clear the search.
guide-back = Back to knowledge index (Esc)
guide-open-view = Open information view
guide-knowledge-intro = Original knowledge categories and case-sensitive menu letters. Select a category to see its current scope, then open the relevant view; closing that view returns here. Only information available to your character is shown. Unavailable statistics are identified explicitly.
guide-topic-basics = Getting started and interface
guide-text-basics = Actions advance game time. Movement, attacks and item use follow their own rules; opening information views does not advance time. Left-click a map cell to travel there; click the map again to stop. Enemies and obstructions interrupt travel. In targeting mode, left-click to confirm a target; in look mode, left-click to move the inspection cursor. You can also move using direction buttons or your active preset. Inventory, abilities, character and tasks can all be opened with buttons, including in narrow windows.
    The interface shows perceived or remembered information. Unidentified items may conceal names and properties; unknown does not mean absent. Complete any mandatory character choice before continuing.
guide-topic-commands = Commands for your preset
guide-topic-movement = Movement, terrain and travel
guide-text-movement = Original/Roguelike: ; then a direction walks normally; - then a direction reverses default pickup for that step. Original , / Roguelike . or numeric 5 stays and applies pickup settings. Original . / Roguelike , then a direction runs; Roguelike uppercase HJKLYUBN runs directly. All presets support Shift plus arrow/numpad directions to run.
    + then a direction or Ctrl plus a direction interacts with the adjacent square: attack a monster, or open, disarm or dig as appropriate. Original j / Roguelike S spikes a door, consuming an inventory spike. An invalid target can still cost an action.
    Backtick selects a local destination; Original J / Roguelike ( resumes travel. Z auto-explores known map boundaries; Original H / Roguelike Ctrl+E travels to the nearest suitable unidentified item. Ctrl+G auto-gets items; _ edits pickup rules. On the surface without a connection, < enters the world map; > returns to the local map, and Enter travels to the selected world destination. At a local connection, < or > uses that connection. Pets accompany you across world-map transitions.
guide-topic-continuous = Continuous actions, counts and cancellation
guide-text-continuous = Original/Roguelike: 0 then a count then a command repeats it; default 99, maximum 9999. Backspace corrects the count; Esc cancels. Original n / Roguelike X repeats the last repeatable command with its selected direction, item and target. Backslash interprets the next key using Original bindings.
    Opening doors/chests, bashing, digging, disarming, closing and adjacent interaction retry up to 99 times when another attempt is needed; a count overrides this. Completion, damage, noteworthy surroundings or a selection prompt interrupts the action. Running follows corridors and stops at junctions and other points requiring attention.
    R accepts a number, * for HP and recoverable resources, or & to also wait for adverse statuses and countdowns (the default). Zero or cancel does not rest. Original S / Roguelike # toggles continuous searching; s searches once. Search mode normally reduces speed by 10.
    Esc, Stop, losing focus or hiding the page stops continuous action. Another game shortcut first stops the action; press again to open its view. Saving also stops and settles actions. Loading does not automatically resume the command queue.
guide-topic-targeting = Targeting and looking
guide-text-targeting = * remembers a target without attacking; on the world map it enters look mode. Original f / Roguelike t fires; spells, items and throwing enter targeting from their own commands. Space, * and + cycle forward; - cycles backward. o selects a free square, m returns to candidates, and p returns to the player. While looking at or targeting a monster, r opens its known details; r or Escape returns to the cursor without advancing time.
    Enter, t, T, ., 5 or 0 confirms; Esc or q cancels. At the start of action targeting, t/T/./5/0 can reuse the old target. Reselect when it disappears, is out of range, or after a floor change or load. Cancellation can retain item costs already incurred; follow the prompt. Original l / Roguelike x looks without attacking.
guide-topic-items = Item selection, inscriptions and equipment
guide-text-items = Enter an item command, then choose an item. Ctrl+P/E/Q/F switches to pack/equipment/quiver/floor when that source is allowed; buttons also switch sources. Inscriptions @ plus a digit assign a general tag; @ plus the Original command letter and a tag assign a command tag. ! plus a command letter or !* requests confirmation. Command tags use Original letters regardless of preset.
    Original W swaps rings; Roguelike uses backslash then W. Two slots swap directly; with more slots, choose two. Bags directly increase inventory capacity and have no P menu. Inspection displays only currently known properties.
guide-topic-magic = Abilities, books and devices
guide-text-magic = The ability page shows costs, failure chance, targeting and proficiency. Original/Roguelike G studies and m casts; Original b browses, while Roguelike uses backslash then b. Original U / Roguelike O focuses racial/class powers. Available study depends on the character and books, with reasons shown for unavailable choices.
    Magic-Eater m opens absorbed devices: W/S/R switches category, X swaps slots, Z inscribes, and Esc cancels. Ordinary devices still use their item commands. Browsing details does not activate an ability.
guide-topic-pets = Pets and riding
guide-text-pets = Original/Roguelike p or the pet-panel button opens the menu. Set a target or follow distance, name or dismiss pets, ride, and control doors, pickup, breeding, offensive spells, teleportation, summoning and player splash damage. Permissions still require the pet's own capabilities.
    Dismissal requires confirmation; Esc exits without changing settings. While riding, two-handed operation relinquishes control and can let the mount move you autonomously. Individual pet listings respect visibility, while upkeep counts the whole party. The world map does not draw local pet positions; the party returns with you.
guide-topic-intel = Maps, intelligence and knowledge
guide-text-intel = All presets: ? opens this manual, ~ opens knowledge, Ctrl+V centers the main map, and Ctrl+F shows the floor feeling. Original/Roguelike M opens overview, Original L / Roguelike W locates, [ lists monsters, and / queries symbols. The map/intelligence buttons provide the same views.
    In locate mode, arrows or preset directions pan half a sector, Ctrl+V returns to the player, and 5 or Esc exits. Symbol queries accept Ctrl+A/U/N/R/M for all known/unique/non-unique/rideable/name. Overview does not reveal unexplored cells; detailed monster properties still require research, and floor feeling is evaluated immediately.
guide-topic-character = Character, combat and tasks
guide-text-character = Original/Roguelike C opens the character page. Overview shows current status; Details breaks down sources, defenses and attacks; Proficiencies lists weapon and other progress; Other shows virtues, mutations and materials. Incomplete equipment knowledge can leave combat values unknown.
    Ctrl+Q opens tasks and Ctrl+P opens messages. ~ gathers these knowledge categories alongside monster, pet, item, material and ability information. Consult tasks for objectives and rewards. Opening knowledge does not accept tasks or claim rewards.
guide-topic-saving = Saving, loading and exiting
guide-text-saving = Ctrl+S creates a named native save; Ctrl+X exits after a successful save. Cancelling the name or a failed save keeps the game open. Save management lists and loads saves; files can also be imported/exported. Loading, starting a new game or returning to the title closes stale knowledge and item selection windows.
    Opening help does not automatically save. Use the save controls to retain progress. Settings, pet permissions and character progress are saved; temporary selected targets and frontend repeat queues do not persist across sessions.
guide-topic-options = Options and automatic pickup rules
guide-text-options = = opens settings for language, input preset, map display and gameplay. Legacy numpad/Vi/WASD presets retain their own bindings rather than the complete RFB command set. Text fields, IME composition and modal dialogs isolate their input from map actions.
    _ opens pickup-rule editing. The first matching rule wins; English and Chinese rules are saved separately and validated on apply. Syntax and import/export controls are in the editor's rule help. Default pickup and rule pickup work independently; special walking reverses only default pickup for one step.
    @ opens custom keys and command recording, Enter opens the command menu, : adds notes, and ) or Ctrl+] exports the current map as PNG/text/HTML. Bindings are saved per preset; backslash bypasses the next key mapping. In Original/Roguelike, double quote selects a register to record the next command; single quote plays a register, with dot for the last command. The editor records multi-step command macros and supports duplication, moving up and deletion; Esc/Stop interrupts playback. Recordings are limited to the current map and session. Notes persist separately on this device and can be exported.
