cfg-macros = Command recording and editing
cfg-macro-help = Choose a register and start recording, then perform actions on the map. Click the recording indicator or press Esc to stop. Macros retain executed single game actions and selected parameters, excluding text input, saves, purchases and permanent character choices. Remove, move up, duplicate or append the last action, up to 256 steps. Playback stops on declined confirmation, damage, an action that cannot continue, a mandatory choice or a floor change; Esc stops subsequent steps.
    These are session command macros, not terminal keystroke strings. All recordings clear on floor changes, wilderness scrolling, loads or new games to prevent reusing unrelated item/monster instance IDs. Running, resting and travel can be replayed as single-command registers, not included in multi-step macros.
